WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.620
Hey, guys, by the way, Joe Biden's going to
be the next president.

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:05.680
There is a really big deal being made out
of a breaking story from investigative reporter

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:12.179
Carl Carl Bernstein of Woodward and Bernstein
fame, about 21 Republican senators who privately

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.100
have been saying anti Trump things.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:22.190
And I am here to tell you, I do not care if
they don't say it publicly and they didn't

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:28.680
say it publicly for the last four years, who
cares that they were privately willing to

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.610
say it to Carl Bernstein?

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:35.989
You know, the there's a couple possibilities
here.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:43.350
Either they weren't saying it publicly because
for a while they supported Trump or they weren't

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:48.670
saying it publicly because they thought that
it was better for their own careers to shut

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.670
their mouths.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.739
Either way, their silence was terrible for
the country for the last four years.

00:00:54.739 --> 00:00:56.339
But we'll come back to that.

00:00:56.339 --> 00:01:02.140
OK, Carl Bernstein tweeted yesterday and dozens
of articles were written about this.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:08.900
The 21 Republican senators who have privately
expressed their disdain for Trump are Portman,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:18.090
Alexander, Sasse, Blunt, Collins, Murkowski,
Cornyn, Thune, Romney, Braun, Young, Tim Scott,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:24.900
Rick Scott, Rubio, Grassley, Burr, Toomey,
McSally, Moran, Roberts and Shelby.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:31.200
Of the people on Bernstein's list, some did
actually criticize Trump publicly, like Ben

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:38.060
Sasse, John Cornyn, occasionally Lisa Murkowski,
certainly Mitt Romney.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:42.970
But I have to tell you, I'm finding myself
completely underwhelmed by this.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.750
Donald Trump has represented an existential
threat to the American system of democracy

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.510
in government and way of life.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:55.450
For four years, a couple of senators have
mildly criticized Donald Trump and even the

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.110
ones that did a little more harshly.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:04.770
Mitt Romney, for example, you know, John Kasich,
within days of Joe Biden winning, they went

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.229
right back to saying, my goal is stopping
Medicare for all.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.430
We've got to stop tax increases.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.049
We've got to deal with the debt.

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:16.090
We have to, you know, reduce business regulation.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:21.709
So if anyone expects me to praise Republican
senators who privately criticize Donald Trump,

00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:23.719
give me a break, guys.

00:02:23.719 --> 00:02:29.079
Imagine if from day one of this presidency
or six months and, you know, whenever it was

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:33.560
abundantly clear to everybody that this was
a disaster, imagine if early on.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.930
Twenty one Republican senators had actually
stood up regularly and strongly criticizing

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:39.930
Donald Trump.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.459
That actually could have made a difference.

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:46.430
Instead, now that Joe Biden has already won,
we hear, oh, twenty one of them said things

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.859
in private about Trump.

00:02:47.859 --> 00:02:49.740
To Carl Bernstein, Give me a break.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:50.740
These people are pathetic.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:57.959
Now, one other aspect of this, Trump and Republicans
love to say it's the left that doesn't allow

00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:04.019
dissenting opinions and it's the left that
doesn't want to engage in the battle of ideas.

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:10.110
These twenty one Republicans, if it is true
that they really didn't like what Donald Trump

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:17.219
was doing, they partially stayed quiet because
they were too scared to say anything.

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:24.120
They were afraid of being outed publicly as
not liking Donald Trump when Trump was still

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.800
riding high.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.519
This is what we call profiles in cowardice.

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:33.489
They aided and abetted Trump.

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:37.109
And if indeed they felt this all along, they
have.

00:03:37.109 --> 00:03:41.569
To be held accountable now for how Donald
Trump has debased democracy for four years

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:46.950
and I mean, think back to impeachment, guys,
everyone but Romney who did vote to convict

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:53.569
on one count on impeachment, if these other
20 Republican senators had voted to convict

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:58.819
Trump on impeachment, they'd have been able
to remove him and they wouldn't have had to

00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:03.059
worry about the repercussions of coming out
against Donald Trump.

00:04:03.059 --> 00:04:04.059
Truly pathetic.

00:04:04.059 --> 00:04:06.299
None of these people should be held up as
heroes.

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:13.340
In fact, what they are is disingenuous, if
indeed nearly half of the Republican senators

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:20.229
in the Senate privately were disturbed, distraught
and against what Donald Trump was doing, what

00:04:20.229 --> 00:04:27.750
they need to be sort of what the what we need
to be pointing the finger to is that they

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:32.180
were completely disingenuous in public and
continuing to support Donald Trump.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.180
Completely pathetic.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.580
I'm glad we learned about it.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.800
These are not heroes.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.800
These are not our friends.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:42.150
And as we saw from Mitt Romney and John Kasich
within 24 hours of the election, they obviously

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:47.740
and predictably, as we've been saying for
years, went right back to the exact type of

00:04:47.740 --> 00:06:02.080
Republicans they were before Donald Trump.

